Subject: Cantor Self Work Update Broker B1 CDrive Production Preparation Plan P0 Dual Hemisphere Review

@ [review_uuid] 9cedac6e-dec8-4415-8b9c-770da5bab457
@ [canonical_uuid] 209c5c94-fd65-4f93-946b-bec56912b29e

& [ConstructiveHemisphere]
  + canonical plan makes the physical P9 operation legible before an operator considers commissioning it
  + exact topology operation ordering ledger identity and upstream bindings reduce later integration ambiguity
  + a reusable verifier gives the future runner a stable contract rather than another prose-only handoff

& [CriticalHemisphere]
  + supplied capacity can become stale and therefore cannot authorize later preparation
  + a plan namespace can be mistaken for an attempt UUID or reserved root
  + planned create steps can be laundered into claims that files or worktrees already exist
  + a compiler controlled by Cantor cannot authenticate its own external commission

& [Reconciliation]
  + status and authority state physical preparation not authorized in every successful form
  + each planned effect is marked later_authority_required and effect account remains zero
  + namespace role is typed plan_namespace and excluded from commission identity
  + later execution must reacquire capacity current carrier topology and all authorities rather than trust this observation

& [Decision]
  + internally_consistent_for_bounded_provider_free_implementation
